"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp`. (#7512)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for manual reader in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7524)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for periodic reader in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7571)\\n\\n- Support `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_INSECURE` and `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_INSECURE` environmental variables in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp`. (#7608)\\n\\n- Add `Enabled` method to the `Processor` interface in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log`. All `Processor` implementations now include an `Enabled` method. (#7639)\\n\\n- The `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.38.0` package. The package contains semantic conventions from the `v1.38.0` version of the OpenTelemetry Semantic Conventions. See the [migration documentation](./semconv/v1.38.0/MIGRATION.md) for information on how to upgrade from `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.37.0.`(#7648)\\n\\n### Changed\\n\\n- `Distinct` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute` is no longer guaranteed to uniquely identify an attribute set. Collisions between `Distinct` values for different Sets are possible with extremely high cardinality (billions of series per instrument), but are highly unlikely. (#7175)\\n\\n- `WithInstrumentationAttributes` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace` synchronously de-duplicates the passed attributes instead of delegating it to the returned `TracerOption`. (#7266)\\n\\n- `WithInstrumentationAttributes` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/meter` synchronously de-duplicates the passed attributes instead of delegating it to the returned `MeterOption`. (#7266)\\n\\n- `WithInstrumentationAttributes` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log` synchronously de-duplicates the passed attributes instead of delegating it to the returned `LoggerOption`. (#7266)\\n\\n- Rename the `OTEL_GO_X_SELF_OBSERVABILITY` environment variable to `OTEL_GO_X_OBSERVABILITY` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/stdout/stdouttrace`. (#7302)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlplog otlploghttp 7512 add experiment observ metric for manual reader in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7524 add experiment observ metric for period reader in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7571 support otel _ export _ otlp _ log _ insecur and otel _ export _ otlp _ insecur environment variabl in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlplog otlploghttp 7608 add enabl method to the processor interfac in go opentelemetri io otel sdk log all processor implement now includ an enabl method 7639 the go opentelemetri io otel semconv v1 38 0 packag the packag contain semant convent from the v1 38 0 version of the opentelemetri semant convent see the migrat document semconv v1 38 0 migrat md for inform on how to upgrad from go opentelemetri io otel semconv v1 37 0 7648 chang distinct in go opentelemetri io otel attribut is no longer guarante to uniqu identifi an attribut set collis between distinct valu for differ set are possibl with extrem high cardin billion of seri per instrument but are high unlik 7175 withinstrumentationattribut in go opentelemetri io otel trace synchron de duplic the pass attribut instead of deleg it to the return traceropt 7266 withinstrumentationattribut in go opentelemetri io otel meter synchron de duplic the pass attribut instead of deleg it to the return meteropt 7266 withinstrumentationattribut in go opentelemetri io otel log synchron de duplic the pass attribut instead of deleg it to the return loggeropt 7266 renam the otel _ go _ x _ self _ observ environ variabl to otel _ go _ x _ observ in go opentelemetri io otel sdk trace go opentelemetri io otel sdk log and go opentelemetri io otel export stdout stdouttrac 7302\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"6a08b40f9cb6a8a6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3997235581991899, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2228107974274142, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81252, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**Tag**: `v1.39.0`  \\n\\n**Published**: 2025-12-08T16:45:46Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n## What's Changed\\n\\n* Drop support for Go 1.23 by @MrAlias in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7274\\n\\n* fix(deps): update module go.opentelemetry.io/collector/pdata to v1.40.0 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7275\\n\\n* chore(deps): update module github.com/securego/gosec/v2 to v2.22.8 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7276\\n\\n* fix(deps): update module github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2 to v2.4.0 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7277\\n\\n* fix(deps): update golang.org/x by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7188\\n\\n* fix(deps