{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"\"custom temporality\" OpenTelemetry Go metric selector"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-03]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-10-10\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3390010099  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-10T13:10:44Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-10T14:04:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-09\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n## Agenda Items\\n\\n### 1. Milestone Progress Review\\n\\n**Current milestone status:**\\n\\n- 17 items still open in the milestone\\n\\n- Most PRs are in review phase or awaiting final approvals\\n\\n**Key items discussed:**\\n\\n#### Expose temporality selector functions\\n\\n- **Status:** Under discussion, may not be accepted in current form\\n\\n- **Discussion:** Tyler and David discussed whether to expose temporality selector parsing functions for configuration\\n\\n- **Decision:** Not recommended for inclusion in SDK. Users should use full OpenTelemetry configuration file format instead of custom configuration snippets\\n\\n- **Rationale:** Want to standardize on OTel configuration format rather than supporting fragmented approaches\\n\\n- **Action:** Tyler to respond with feedback about standardization preference\\n\\n#### Prometheus Exporter Migration\\n\\n- **Status:** Implementation complete, needs deprecation decision\\n\\n- **Discussion:** Need to decide on deprecating existing configuration options\\n\\n- **Decision:** Tyler supports deprecation before marking as stable\\n\\n- **Next steps:** Handle in next milestone\\n\\n#### Error Handling for Prometheus\\n\\n- **Status:** PR ready for review, waiting for conversation resolution\\n\\n- **Action:** David to review and potentially merge\\n\\n#### High mutex contention in metric sums\\n\\n- **Status:** Resolved via PR #7427\\n\\n- **Action:** Close issue\\n\\n### 2. Optimization Work Discussion\\n\\n**David's current work:**\\n\\n- Implementing lockless exponential histogram\\n\\n- Fun and challenging optimization project\\n\\n- Building on previous optimization PRs\\n\\n**PR Reviews needed:**\\n\\n- **PR #7474:** Exemplar reservoir optimization (approved by Tyler, needs second approval)\\n\\n- **PR #7443:** Histogram optimization (needs review, has race condition issue identified)\\n\\n**Technical discussion on PR #7443:**\\n\\n- Tyler identified potential race condition in min/max tracking with `isSet` flag\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 03 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 1010 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3390010099 author pellar creat 2025 10 10t13 10 44z updat 2025 10 10t14 04 27z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 09 attende tyler yahn david ashpol bryan boreham agenda item 1 mileston progress review current mileston status 17 item still open in the mileston most pr are in review phase or await final approv key item discuss expos tempor selector function status under discuss may not be accept in current form discuss tyler and david discuss whether to expos tempor selector pars function for configur decis not recommend for inclus in sdk user should use full opentelemetri configur file format instead of custom configur snippet rational want to standard on otel configur format rather than support fragment approach action tyler to respond with feedback about standard prefer prometheus export migrat status implement complet need deprec decis discuss need to decid on deprec exist configur option decis tyler support deprec befor mark a stabl next step handl in next mileston error handl for prometheus status pr readi for review wait for convers resolut action david to review and potenti merg high mutex content in metric sum status resolv via pr 7427 action close issu 2 optim work discuss david s current work implement lockless exponenti histogram fun and challeng optim project build on previous optim pr pr review need pr 7474 exemplar reservoir optim approv by tyler need second approv pr 7443 histogram optim need review ha race condit issu identifi technic discuss on pr 7443 tyler identifi potenti race condit in min max track with isset flag\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"87365f6e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"id\": \"22374080d99b56a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36570776163434904, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.21052631662049864, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7277978, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"87365f6e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3423, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:31\", \"token_count\": 796, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"*   David also mentioned ongoing work on exponential histograms and a simpler \\\"last value\\\" PR that shares code with the histogram one.\\n\\n*   Tyler expressed a strong desire to merge the histogram reservoir PR in the current milestone due to its significant performance improvement and encouraged attendees to review it.\\n\\n**6. Milestone Check-in and Release Goals**\\n\\n*   Tyler conducted a check-in on the v1.39.0 milestones for [Otel](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/milestone/74) and [Contrib](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/milestone/33).\\n\\n*   **Exposed Temporality Selector Function PR:** Tyler noted that a previous SIG meeting concluded this PR was API pollution and should be closed. He will draft a comment and close it today.\\n\\n*   **Simple Span Processor (Tracing):** This PR needs another round of reviews but is considered straightforward and should remain in the milestone.\\n\\n*   **OTLP Metric GRPC Exporter Metrics:** This PR has been open for a while and needs more iteration. It might be moved out of the current milestone if a release push occurs.\\n\\n*   **Metrics SDK Standard Out Metrics Exporter & Standard Log Exporter:** Both PRs lack follow-up from their original authors and significant work is still needed. They are candidates for being bumped from the milestone.\\n\\n*   **Overall Release Strategy:** Tyler proposed making a release before KubeCon (less than a month away) and urged everyone to prioritize reviews for the critical PRs to achieve this goal.\\n\\n**7. KubeCon Discussion**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** asked if there was anything specific to announce or discuss at KubeCon.\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** mentioned the extended attributes merge in specification and product as something he'd like to highlight, though it's not ready.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** expressed interest in showcasing the new observability features.\\n\\n*   David suggested working towards a stable release of the HTTP instrumentation in Contrib. Tyler agreed it was a good idea but noted the significant work involved due to existing \\\"cruft\\\" and potential needs for API restructuring.\\n\\n**8. Tyler's Side Project (OTLP Exporter Error Types)**\\n\\n*   Tyler shared that he's been working on introducing new, custom error types for OTLP exporters to provide clearer, more unified error messages. This involves distinguishing between HTTP/gRPC errors, partial errors, and warnings. He has a prototype integrated for Otel Trace gRPC. While not critical, it improves observability and user understanding of errors.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"david also mention ongo work on exponenti histogram and a simpler last valu pr that share code with the histogram one tyler express a strong desir to merg the histogram reservoir pr in the current mileston due to it signific perform improv and encourag attende to review it 6 mileston check in and releas goal tyler conduct a check in on the v1 39 0 mileston for otel http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go mileston 74 and contrib http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib mileston 33 expos tempor selector function pr tyler note that a previous sig meet conclud this pr wa api pollut and should be close he will draft a comment and close it today simpl span processor trace this pr need anoth round of review but is consid straightforward and should remain in the mileston otlp metric grpc export metric this pr ha been open for a while and need more iter it might be move out of the current mileston if a releas push occur metric sdk standard out metric export standard log export both pr lack follow up from their origin author and signific work is still need they are candid for be bump from the mileston overal releas strategi tyler propos make a releas befor kubecon less than a month away and urg everyon to priorit review for the critic pr to achiev this goal 7 kubecon discuss david ashpol ask if there wa anyth specif to announc or discus at kubecon robert paj ą k mention the extend attribut merg in specif and product a someth he d like to highlight though it s not readi tyler yahn express interest in showcas the new observ featur david suggest work toward a stabl releas of the http instrument in contrib tyler agre it wa a good idea but note the signific work involv due to exist cruft and potenti need for api restructur 8 tyler s side project otlp export error type tyler share that he s been work on introduc new custom error type for otlp export to provid clearer more unifi error messag this involv distinguish between http grpc error partial error and warn he ha a prototyp integr for otel trace grpc while not critic it improv observ and user understand of error\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"fc13fa8c97d8e3a2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35852940363434904, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.21052631662049864, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70386994, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:25\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-01]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-10-10\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3389930076  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-10T12:53:12Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-10T12:54:14Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-09-25\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn.\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham.\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole).\\n\\n- Owen Williams.\\n\\n- Robert Pająk.\\n\\n## Announcements\\n\\n- go.opentelemetry.io certificate incident:\\n\\n  - Website experienced downtime due to a certificate issuance problem.\\n\\n  - Issue has been remediated; if problems persist, open an issue or ask in Slack.\\n\\n  - A post-mortem will be published to cover root cause and the broader incident.\\n\\n  - Apologies for the disruption; steps will be taken to prevent recurrence.\\n\\n- Events:\\n\\n  - KubeCon EU likely in Amsterdam next year; some attendees considering talks.\\n\\n  - Talk idea noted: “Parsing Protobuf at gigabytes per second — and other fantasies.”\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-01]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-10-10\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3389930076  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-10T12:53:12Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-10T12:54:14Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-09-25\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn.\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham.\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole).\\n\\n- Owen Williams.\\n\\n- Robert Pająk.\\n\\n## Milestone Check-in\\n\\n- Why does cardinality limit add performance overhead to metric measurements?\\n\\n  - Status: Needs benchmarking to assess/confirm.\\n\\n  - Assignee: David Ashpole volunteered.\\n\\n  - Note: If it takes longer than expected, may unassign and remove from milestone.\\n\\n- Expose temporality selector functions:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 01 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 1010 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3389930076 author pellar creat 2025 10 10t12 53 12z updat 2025 10 10t12 54 14z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 09 25 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham david ashpol dashpol owen william robert paj ą k announc go opentelemetri io certif incid websit experienc downtim due to a certif issuanc problem issu ha been remedi if problem persist open an issu or ask in slack a post mortem will be publish to cover root caus and the broader incid apolog for the disrupt step will be taken to prevent recurr event kubecon eu like in amsterdam next year some attende consid talk talk idea note pars protobuf at gigabyt per second and other fantasi sourc id src note 01 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 1010 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3389930076 author pellar creat 2025 10 10t12 53 12z updat 2025 10 10t12 54 14z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 09 25 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham david ashpol dashpol owen william robert paj ą k mileston check in whi doe cardin limit add perform overhead to metric measur status need benchmark to assess confirm assigne david ashpol volunt note if it take longer than expect may unassign and remov from mileston expos tempor selector function\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"id\": \"532c41285ab18d1f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3519101901514312, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17543859735918746, \"vector_similarity\": 0.76367724, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4478, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:33\", \"token_count\": 1509, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Improve performance of histogram `Record` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric` when min and max are disabled using `NoMinMax`. (#7306)\\n\\n- Improve error handling for dropped data during translation by using `prometheus.NewInvalidMetric` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus`. ⚠️ **Breaking Change:** Previously, these cases were only logged and scrapes succeeded. Now, when translation would drop data (e.g., invalid label/value), the exporter emits a `NewInvalidMetric`, and Prometheus scrapes **fail with HTTP 500** by default. To preserve the prior behavior (scrapes succeed while errors are logged), configure your Prometheus HTTP handler with: `promhttp.HandlerOpts{ ErrorHandling: promhttp.ContinueOnError }`. (#7363)\\n\\n- Replace fnv hash with xxhash in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute` for better performance. (#7371)\\n\\n- The default `TranslationStrategy` in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/prometheus` is changed from `otlptranslator.NoUTF8EscapingWithSuffixes` to `otlptranslator.UnderscoreEscapingWithSuffixes`. (#7421)\\n\\n- Improve performance of concurrent measurements in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7427)\\n\\n- Include W3C TraceFlags (bits 0–7) in the OTLP `Span.Flags` field in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp` and `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc`. (#7438)\\n\\n- The `ErrorType` function in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.37.0` now handles custom error types.\\n\\n  If an error implements an `ErrorType() string` method, the return value of that method will be used as the error type. (#7442)\\n\\n### Fixed\\n\\n- Fix `WithInstrumentationAttributes` options in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log` to properly merge attributes when passed multiple times instead of replacing them. Attributes with duplicate keys will use the last value passed. (#7300)\\n\\n- The equality of `attribute.Set` when using the `Equal` method is not affected by the user overriding the empty set pointed to by `attribute.EmptySet` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute`. (#7357)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"improv perform of histogram record in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric when min and max are disabl use nominmax 7306 improv error handl for drop data dure translat by use prometheus newinvalidmetr in go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus break chang previous these case were onli log and scrape succeed now when translat would drop data e g invalid label valu the export emit a newinvalidmetr and prometheus scrape fail with http 500 by default to preserv the prior behavior scrape succeed while error are log configur your prometheus http handler with promhttp handleropt errorhandl promhttp continueonerror 7363 replac fnv hash with xxhash in go opentelemetri io otel attribut for better perform 7371 the default translationstrategi in go opentelemetri io export prometheus is chang from otlptransl noutf8escapingwithsuffixes to otlptransl underscoreescapingwithsuffix 7421 improv perform of concurr measur in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7427 includ w3c traceflag bit 0 7 in the otlp span flag field in go opentelemetri io export otlp otlptrac otlptracehttp and go opentelemetri io export otlp otlptrac otlptracegrpc 7438 the errortyp function in go opentelemetri io otel semconv v1 37 0 now handl custom error type if an error implement an errortyp string method the return valu of that method will be use a the error type 7442 fix fix withinstrumentationattribut option in go opentelemetri io otel trace go opentelemetri io otel metric and go opentelemetri io otel log to proper merg attribut when pass multipl time instead of replac them attribut with duplic key will use the last valu pass 7300 the equal of attribut set when use the equal method is not affect by the user overrid the empti set point to by attribut emptyset in go opentelemetri io otel attribut 7357\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"2fc8f714ea7b265d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3421616181514312, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17543859735918746, \"vector_similarity\": 0.731182, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"\\tvalues                  sync.Map\\n\\n\\tlen                     atomic.Int64\\n\\n```\\n\\n**dashpole** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/aggregate.go` — 2025-10-03T15:23:10Z\\n\\nfair enough.  I felt it was more readable to have it accept the temporality than to pass a bool, but I can work on refactoring.\\n\\n**dashpole** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T15:25:53Z\\n\\nnice.  lgtm\\n\\n**dashpole** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T15:27:00Z\\n\\nyes\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T15:32:21Z\\n\\nSorry, didn't make it clear in my suggestion. This needs to change based on pre-increment.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\tif loaded {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Someone else created this entry while we reserved a slot.\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Decrement our reserved count since we didn't actually add a new entry.\\n\\n\\t\\t\\ts.len[hotIdx].Add(-1)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**dashpole** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T16:00:07Z\\n\\nActually, I remembered why I didn't take this approach:  It introduces a new race condition where we can overflow even if we didn't create too many attribute sets.  Worse, we can end up splitting a single attribute set's observations between the attribute set and the overflow set.\\n\\nSuppose we have an attribute set limit of 2.  We get 2 concurrent measure calls to the empty attribute set.\\n\\nThe first measure call increments len to 1.  Then, before the element is added to the map, the second measure call increments len to 2.  The first measure call will be written to the empty attribute set (correct!).  The second measure call will be written to the overflow set (incorrect!).\\n\\nIMO, this is worse than the possibility to exceed the attribute limit.\\n\\n**dashpole** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T16:02:38Z\\n\\nUnresolving, and I reverted the suggestion.  I don't think this works.  See https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427#discussion_r2402472887\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"valu sync map len atom int64 dashpol on sdk metric intern aggreg aggreg go 2025 10 03t15 23 10z fair enough i felt it wa more readabl to have it accept the tempor than to pas a bool but i can work on refactor dashpol on sdk metric intern aggreg sum go 2025 10 03t15 25 53z nice lgtm dashpol on sdk metric intern aggreg sum go 2025 10 03t15 27 00z yes mralia on sdk metric intern aggreg sum go 2025 10 03t15 32 21z sorri didn t make it clear in my suggest this need to chang base on pre increment suggest if load someon els creat this entri while we reserv a slot decrement our reserv count sinc we didn t actual add a new entri s len hotidx add 1 dashpol on sdk metric intern aggreg sum go 2025 10 03t16 00 07z actual i rememb whi i didn t take this approach it introduc a new race condit where we can overflow even if we didn t creat too mani attribut set wors we can end up split a singl attribut set s observ between the attribut set and the overflow set suppos we have an attribut set limit of 2 we get 2 concurr measur call to the empti attribut set the first measur call increment len to 1 then befor the element is ad to the map the second measur call increment len to 2 the first measur call will be written to the empti attribut set correct the second measur call will be written to the overflow set incorrect imo this is wors than the possibl to exceed the attribut limit dashpol on sdk metric intern aggreg sum go 2025 10 03t16 02 38z unresolv and i revert the suggest i don t think this work see http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 discuss _ r2402472887\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"id\": \"85248e11ec6386cb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33118831566851337, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14035087809787627, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77647567, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 37741, \"chunk_count\": 26, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:02\", \"token_count\": 14705, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-04]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics to improve sum performance (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7427)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-29T14:36:56Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-14T14:40:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-10-07T13:40:23Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_counter_syncmap` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +437 / -121 across 14 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area:metrics  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.39.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (18)\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `CHANGELOG.md` — 2025-10-02T17:55:27Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n- Improve performance of concurrent measurements in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7427)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/aggregate.go` — 2025-10-03T00:03:10Z\\n\\nPassing the temporality only to then parse it below and make a decision here seems like a bad smell. I'm more inclined to refactoring the Sum in some way to better address this and remove the control param being passed here.\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T15:10:13Z\\n\\nA pre-increment approach with rollback may address this.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\t// Pre-increment, reserve a slot first.\\n\\n\\t\\tnewLen := s.len[hotIdx].Add(1)\\n\\n\\t\\tif s.aggLimit > 0 && newLen >= int64(s.aggLimit) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// We exceeded the limit, decrement back and use overflow\\n\\n\\t\\t\\ts.len[hotIdx].Add(-1)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfltrAttr = overflowSet\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n```\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T15:14:24Z\\n\\nSplitting this into a type dedicated to cumulative values seems appropriate. It would have fields like this right?\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 04 pull request use sync map and atom to improv sum perform open telemetri opentelemetri go 7427 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 author dashpol creat 2025 09 29t14 36 56z updat 2025 10 14t14 40 27z collect 2