il\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Status: PR exists; default temporality aggregation functions were not exposed; proposal includes a string-based “temporality select.”\\n\\n  - Concern: Replacing functions via string selector raised concerns.\\n\\n  - Next: No recent activity; likely to wait and potentially move out of the milestone.\\n\\n- Optimized locking for metric aggregation:\\n\\n  - Status: Work in progress by David; awaiting one more testing PR before starting locking improvements.\\n\\n  - Context: Approach reviewed informally with Josh McDonald; thought reasonably good.\\n\\n  - Testing PR: “Add concurrent-safe tests for metric aggregation” needs more reviews.\\n\\n  - Notes: A test-run issue caused confusion around time ordering; not a fundamental `time.Now` issue. Go 1.25 testing time manipulation may help if needed.\\n\\n- Exporter: Prometheus migrate to new configuration options:\\n\\n  - Status: On David’s list.\\n\\n  - Scope: Expected to be a one-line default change; no “Help Wanted” needed.\\n\\n- Improved error handling:\\n\\n  - Status: PR was in draft and author became inactive.\\n\\n  - Decision: Remove from milestone; consider pinging the author. Should not block release.\\n\\n- High mutex contention in metric sums:\\n\\n  - Status: Assigned to David; actively being fixed.\\n\\n- Observability packages:\\n\\n  - Status: Multiple PRs open and being reworked.\\n\\n  - Release impact: Not critical for upcoming release; if they block, move them out.\\n\\n  - Activity: Some PRs show movement; Tyler is actively working on one; others have limited updates.\\n\\n- Prometheus exporter: Optimize return times:\\n\\n  - Status: Worth review for those working on observability metrics.\\n\\n  - Context: Already merged for the standard trace exporter.\\n\\n  - Note: Awaiting minimum time requirement (~23 minutes) before completion.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-01]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-10-10\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3389930076  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-10T12:53:12Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-10T12:54:14Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-09-25\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn.\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham.\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"status pr exist default tempor aggreg function were not expos propos includ a string base tempor select concern replac function via string selector rais concern next no recent activ like to wait and potenti move out of the mileston optim lock for metric aggreg status work in progress by david await one more test pr befor start lock improv context approach review inform with josh mcdonald thought reason good test pr add concurr safe test for metric aggreg need more review note a test run issu caus confus around time order not a fundament time now issu go 1 25 test time manipul may help if need export prometheus migrat to new configur option status on david s list scope expect to be a one line default chang no help want need improv error handl status pr wa in draft and author becam inact decis remov from mileston consid ping the author should not block releas high mutex content in metric sum status assign to david activ be fix observ packag status multipl pr open and be rework releas impact not critic for upcom releas if they block move them out activ some pr show movement tyler is activ work on one other have limit updat prometheus export optim return time status worth review for those work on observ metric context alreadi merg for the standard trace export note await minimum time requir 23 minut befor complet sourc id src note 01 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 1010 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3389930076 author pellar creat 2025 10 10t12 53 12z updat 2025 10 10t12 54 14z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 09 25 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham david ashpol dashpol\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"id\": \"bab18cd51375b357\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3180491736685134, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14035087809787627, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73267853, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4478, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:33\", \"token_count\": 1509, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-06-16T07:44:04Z\\n\\nI created \\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7470\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6904\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6903\\n\\nI think it might be also good to add some \\\"error recording\\\" recommendations in https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, we should first clarify it on the semantic conventions side.\\n\\n>  I believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nThis seems not compliant with https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-metrics\\n\\n> Errors that were retried or handled (allowing an operation to complete gracefully) SHOULD NOT be recorded on spans or metrics that describe this operation.\\n\\nCurrently, the only use case I see the only use of `span.RecordError` to use it for \\\"unhandled exceptions\\\" (which for Go can be done in the SDK) and to record multiple errors like here:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go#L119-L124\\n\\nI do not find the semantic conventions clear and probably some work is also needed there.\\n\\nCC @lmolkova\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-03T20:45:58Z\\n\\nSorry for joining the discussion late.\\n\\n@pellared I am confused about what we should do to handle errors, especially **non-terminating errors**. Should we do nothing if we encounter an error?\\n\\nFor instance, when facing code like this, do we do nothing for the error we receive?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"pellar 2025 06 16t07 44 04z i creat http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7470 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6904 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6903 i think it might be also good to add some error record recommend in http pkg go dev go opentelemetri io otel trace howev we should first clarifi it on the semant convent side i believ span recorderror http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace a